WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.442
When the same transformation is used more than once, it is often a good idea to place that logic inside a function.

00:00:07.442 --> 00:00:14.782
In the example, the add order size function receives a DataFrame, creates an order-size category,

00:00:14.782 --> 00:00:17.432
and returns the updated DataFrame.

00:00:17.432 --> 00:00:22.197
Pipe lets us insert that function naturally into a Pandas method chain.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.932
This approach can make longer workflows easier to read and maintain.

00:00:26.932 --> 00:00:34.697
Instead of placing twenty operations in one large block, you can create several small functions with clear names.

00:00:34.697 --> 00:00:40.732
For example, one function might clean column names, another might create categories,

00:00:40.732 --> 00:00:43.372
and another might calculate a report.

00:00:43.372 --> 00:00:49.727
Run the code and follow how the DataFrame moves through the pipe function and then into sort values.

00:00:49.727 --> 00:00:54.922
A useful rule is to keep each function focused on one clear responsibility.

00:00:54.922 --> 00:00:59.413
Small functions are easier to understand, reuse, and test.
